-talich-exits-1st-half-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-22T01:42:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brandon's two TD runs lift No. 9 Tennessee past LSU","description":"Tennessee's stifling defense shut down LSU, and the No. 9 Volunteers beat the Tigers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:30:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA loses Ty Dieffenbach to injury, stays resolute with B1G title game in reach","description":"UCLA coach Bob Chesney said his message to the Bruins was, \"Nobody hang your head,\" despite losing QB Ty Dieffenbach to injury in a tough, 18-16 defeat at Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:41:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5132635/jayden-jackson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayden_Jackson"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jayden Jackson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayden_Jackson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:15Z","intro":"Jayden Jackson is an American college football defensive tackle for the Oklahoma Sooners.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Jackson attended IMG Academy in Bradenton, Florida. He was selected to play in the 2024 Polynesian Bowl. He committed to the University of Oklahoma to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Jackson entered his true freshman season at Oklahoma in 2024 as a starter becoming the first true freshman defensive lineman to start for the Sooners since Tommie Harris in 2001. Overall, he started 10 of 13 games, recording 30 tackles and two sacks. He returned to Oklahoma for his sophomore year in 2025."}]}}